/*
  KOTH Timer firmware v0.4.0
  Standalone release candidate
  Target board: Arduino Nano ESP32 (NORA-W106)

  Core game rules:
  - A team counts down only while exactly one team button is held.
  - Both buttons held = contested; neither team scores.
  - No buttons held = no scoring.
  - The match ends when either team's timer reaches zero.

  Standalone controls:
  - Local Wi-Fi admin UI at http://10.10.10.1/
  - Manual physical start: hold both team buttons for 5 seconds.
  - Referee time adjustment from the web UI.
  - Team identification mode while stopped.

  Battery protection:
  - 10k / 10k divider on A0.
  - Critical low-battery warning below 3.40 V.
  - A running match is frozen and saved to NVS at critical battery.
  - A saved match is restored paused after a battery swap/reboot.

  Notes:
  - The access point intentionally does NOT use captive-portal / automatic
    browser launching. Join "KOTH-Timer", then open http://10.10.10.1/.
  - Buzzer support is optional. The timer works normally with no buzzer fitted.\n  - If fitted, use a 3-pin active buzzer; patterns are rhythmic, not pitched.
*/

